msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:804
msgid "Violation: every minute in which the IP exceeded a limit, and every fake Googlebot. The trap blocks immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:805
msgid "Block duration (minutes):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:806
msgid "Early check: block known bots before the theme and the other plugins load"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:806
msgid "Adds the small file wp-content/mu-plugins/scrapelock-early.php, which stops blocked IPs and referrers, temporarily blocked IPs and User-Agents in the bot list with less server load. Search engines, logged-in users, forms and feeds are left to the normal check. It is removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:808
msgid "The file could not be created (the server does not allow direct file writes to wp-content/mu-plugins). The normal check works as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:811
msgid "Pre-cache check: apply the page limit and blocks also to pages served from the page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:811
msgid "Page caches such as WP Rocket serve stored pages before any plugin loads, so a bot that looks like a browser could read them without a limit. This adds one line at the top of wp-config.php that loads a small check before the cache: always-blocked IPs, temporarily blocked IPs and the “Pages per minute” limit. Counters are kept in APCu or in a folder of the uploads directory (uploads/scrapelock). Search engines, logged-in users, forms, wp-admin and the REST API are left to the normal check. The line and the files are removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:815
msgid "Keep the block log for:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:821
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1313
